// Getgud PSAT/NMSQT Practice Test 1 — a committed, hand-reviewed selection of
// College Board question-bank ids from the PSAT/NMSQT & PSAT 10 bank.
// Generated by `pnpm design:exam --exam=psat-practice-1 --seed=getgud-psat-practice-1`
// (design constants live in scripts/design-exam.ts under DESIGNS["psat-practice-1"]),
// then reviewed. Re-verify with `pnpm design:exam --exam=psat-practice-1 --verify`
// after any manual edit to an id list. Every id is a College Board natural key
// (see ./index.ts), so this exact test runs identically on any self-hosted
// instance whose bank includes these ids.
//
// Structure (digital PSAT/NMSQT, PSAT 10 and PSAT 8/9 share this blueprint):
//   - Reading & Writing: 2 modules x 27 questions x 32 min. Math: 2 modules x 22
//     questions x 35 min. 10-minute break. 98 questions, 2h14m of testing.
//     Module 1 is a broad mix; its result routes to an easier or harder
//     Module 2 (see routingThreshold below).
//   - Scale: each section 160-760, total 320-1520. PSAT/NMSQT juniors also get
//     the NMSC Selection Index, (2 x RW + Math) / 10, 48-228 — derived at
//     render time (spec.ts's nmscSelectionIndex), never stored.
//
// Layout (what "exactly like the real PSAT" means here):
//   - RW is laid out by SKILL GROUP, ascending difficulty within each group, so
//     difficulty resets at each new group: Words in Context, Text Structure &
//     Purpose, Cross-Text Connections, Central Ideas & Details, Command of
//     Evidence (textual, then quantitative), Inferences, then Standard English
//     Conventions (Boundaries and Form/Structure/Sense MIXED, ordered by
//     difficulty only), Transitions, Rhetorical Synthesis last. Domain shares
//     per module are 8/7/7/5 (Craft & Structure ~28%, Information & Ideas
//     ~26%, Conventions ~26%, Expression of Ideas ~20%).
//   - Math has no domain grouping: ascending difficulty across the whole
//     module. 6 of 22 per module are student-produced responses, at positions
//     5, 6, 11, 12, 17, 22 — College Board's official PSAT Practice Test #3
//     answer key puts them at 6, 7, 13, 14, 20, 21, 27 of 27 (26%).
//   - Math domain mix follows College Board's PSAT alignment table (Algebra
//     ~35%, Advanced Math ~32.5%, Problem-Solving & Data Analysis ~20%,
//     Geometry & Trig ~12.5%): Module 1 is 8/7/4/3, each Module 2 is 7/7/5/3.
//     The PSAT bank has no circles, unit-circle trig or "evaluating
//     statistical claims" items, so drawing from it enforces PSAT-only scope.
//
// Approximations, stated plainly (same stance as the SAT blueprints):
//   - All 98 questions are scored. The real test has ~2 unscored pretest items
//     per module, indistinguishable to the taker; this app has no pretest bank,
//     and the 27/22 module lengths already include those slots.
//   - routingThreshold is a raw-count stand-in for College Board's IRT-based
//     routing (17/27 RW, 14/22 Math, ~63-64%), same as the SAT exams.
//   - Scaled scores: the upper tables average the midpoint of College Board's
//     official raw-to-scale ranges from the paper-form PSAT/NMSQT Practice
//     Tests #1, #2 and #3 (satsuite.collegeboard.org scoring guides; the three
//     forms differ most at low raw scores, so they are averaged), rescaled
//     from those 66 / 54 raw points to this test's 54 / 44 by linear
//     interpolation and rounded to the nearest 10. This is an approximation of
//     the adaptive test's IRT scoring, not a reproduction of it.
//   - The lower-path cap has NO official PSAT anchor (the SAT's 580 Math figure
//     is from the SAT Technical Manual). It reuses the SAT blueprint's method:
//     the lower table tracks the upper table up to raw 39 (RW) / 30 (Math) and
//     holds that value after, so a perfect easier-module-2 run tops out where
//     a strong-but-imperfect harder-module-2 run lands (RW 540, Math 500).
//   - Difficulty bands (scoreBand) are the PSAT bank's own; the Module 1 /
//     lower / upper band curves reuse sat-practice-1's column shapes.

